Mark changes of audio devices in the macOS audio engine device

WebRTC patch 0011 makes the echo controller anew at the next start of recording after a
change of audio devices. WebRTC-SDK's AudioEngineDevice, the audio device module of the
macOS framework, marks one (MarkAudioDevicesChanged) when the system's list of devices
changes, when the default output or input changes (after its debounce), and when an output
or input other than the current one is chosen. Not marked: an output switching its data
source on the same device (the headphone jack of Macs that show headphones and internal
speakers as one device), which neither the list nor the default shows; and the engine's
configuration changes, which it may also post as it reconfigures itself.

